For all dilution rates, measurements of residual glucose, biomass concentration, oxygen and carbon dioxide concentrations in the offgas were performed. In addition the total organic carbon (TOC) concentration of the culture filtrate was determined in order to verify whether significant amounts of by-products were formed. From these measurements, it appeared that recoveries of the carbon and degree of reduction were >90 % and thus the biomass specific rates were calculated and reconciled (Table 2). Moreover, the biomass elemental composition was determined from several chemostat samples and shown to be 27.3 ± 0.2 g/mol (C1H1.8N0.12O0.6) (Table S3).Table 2
